{"task_id": "HumanEval/34", "solution": "import doctest\ndef unique(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return sorted unique elements in a list\n    >>> unique([5, 3, 5, 2, 3, 3, 9, 0, 123])\n    [0, 2, 3, 5, 9, 123]\n    \"\"\"\n    # Try the fast hashable path first (e.g., ints, strings).\n    try:\n        return sorted(dict.fromkeys(l))\n    except TypeError:\n        # Fallback for unhashable elements (e.g., lists).\n        seen = []\n        for x in l:\n            if not any(x == y for y in seen):\n                seen.append(x)\n        return sorted(seen)"}
