{"task_id": "HumanEval/129", "solution": "import heapq\nfrom typing import List\ndef minPath(grid: List[List[int]], k: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the lexicographically minimum path of length k in the grid.\n    The grid is N x N and contains a permutation of 1..N*N.\n    Movement is allowed to adjacent cells (up, down, left, right).\n    Revisiting cells is allowed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not grid or not grid[0]:\n        return []\n\n    n = len(grid)\n    # Directions for the four neighbors.\n    dirs = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n\n    def neighbors(r: int, c: int) -> List[tuple]:\n        \"\"\"Return (nr, nc, val) for each valid adjacent cell.\"\"\"\n        res = []\n        for dr, dc in dirs:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if 0 <= nr < n and 0 <= nc < n:\n                res.append((nr, nc, grid[nr][nc]))\n        return res\n\n    # Find the cell with the smallest value (value 1).\n    start_r, start_c = 0, 0\n    for r in range(n):\n        for c in range(n):\n            if grid[r][c] == 1:\n                start_r, start_c = r, c\n                break\n        if start_r != 0:\n            break\n\n    path = [grid[start_r][start_c]]\n    cur_r, cur_c = start_r, start_c\n\n    # Greedy: at each step choose the neighbor with the smallest value.\n    for _ in range(k - 1):\n        heap = []\n        for nr, nc, val in neighbors(cur_r, cur_c):\n            heapq.heappush(heap, (val, nr, nc))\n        # heapq.heappop returns the smallest element.\n        nr, nc, val = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        path.append(val)\n        cur_r, cur_c = nr, nc\n\n    return path"}
